## Code Block Formatting

When including any code or content snippets, you MUST use this format:
```path/to/Something.blah#L123-456
(content goes here)
```
The `#L123-456` means the line number range 123 through 456, and the path/to/Something.blah
is a path in the project. This is the ONLY valid way to format code blocks. When providing
marketing content, use appropriate file extensions (.md, .html, .json for structured data, etc.).

